1
00:01:56,936 --> 00:01:58,936


2
00:01:58,960 --> 00:01:59,360
Alright!

3
00:01:59,913 --> 00:02:00,179
Next!

4
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,080
Hah!

5
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:02,100
Your Highness!

6
00:02:02,214 --> 00:02:03,214
Here goes!

7
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:10,300
Bullseye!

8
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:11,700
All five hit!

9
00:02:12,275 --> 00:02:13,780
They didn't hit the center, though.

10
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:14,640
Alright!

11
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,440
One more time!

12
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:17,653
There!

13
00:02:23,419 --> 00:02:23,813
Nice!

14
00:02:24,015 --> 00:02:25,380
All five right in the center!

15
00:02:27,446 --> 00:02:27,973
Wait, no!

16
00:02:28,394 --> 00:02:30,220
The ones in the center aren't mine!

17
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,320
Huh?

18
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,381
Could it be... hm?

19
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,640
Over there!

20
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:43,180
Who's there?!

21
00:02:50,226 --> 00:02:50,760
Right!

22
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:51,180
Opal!

23
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:51,853
Go!

24
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:13,800
Hey!

25
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,860
Sapphire!

26
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,014
Who goes there!

27
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:17,466
You!

28
00:03:19,834 --> 00:03:21,700
Oh, it's Prince Franz!

29
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,760
Sorry!

30
00:03:22,761 --> 00:03:24,773
I wanted to meet you somewhere alone!

31
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,700
Feisty as ever, I see!

32
00:03:28,835 --> 00:03:29,880
You tomboy princess!

33
00:03:30,035 --> 00:03:31,220
I'm not a princess!

34
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,946
I told you, I'm a prince!

35
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:34,250
There's no one around!

36
00:03:34,614 --> 00:03:36,100
You don't have to hide it from me!

37
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,280
Princess Sapphire!

38
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,960
Sapphire is a boy!

39
00:03:38,985 --> 00:03:39,820
A boy!

40
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,766
No matter what anyone says, a boy!

41
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:42,920
Here!

42
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:45,110
Wait, isn't this a pen?!

43
00:03:45,515 --> 00:03:46,880
Don't bring random stuff into this!

44
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:48,230
Never mind that, just take it!

45
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,693
Here!

46
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,800
Paper and ink!

47
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:51,920
So, you're a boy, right?

48
00:03:52,215 --> 00:03:55,260
Then write Sapphire is a boy right here!

49
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:56,500
What on earth for?!

50
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,200
It's a magical pen!

51
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,640
Now, write what I told you!

52
00:04:01,353 --> 00:04:03,733
<i>Sapphire is a boy.</i>

53
00:04:04,313 --> 00:04:05,520
You meant to write <i>Sapphire is a boy</i>, right?

54
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:08,260
But take a close look at what you wrote!

55
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,680
<i>Sapphire is a girl</i>!

56
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,180
See?

57
00:04:12,375 --> 00:04:14,560
You wrote <i>girl</i> yourself!

58
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,500
That's strange!

59
00:04:15,586 --> 00:04:17,466
But I wrote <i>boy</i>!

60
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
One more time!

61
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:21,113
<i>Sapphire is a boy</i>... 

62
00:04:21,877 --> 00:04:23,260
<i>Sapphire is a girl</i>!

63
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:25,440
Why do I keep writing <i>girl</i>?!

64
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,166
Because you ARE a girl!

65
00:04:29,763 --> 00:04:33,093
Sapphire, a great doctor gave me that magic pen!

66
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,240
You can't write lies with it!

67
00:04:35,425 --> 00:04:38,260
Even the biggest liar can only write the truth with that pen!

68
00:04:39,175 --> 00:04:41,666
You know, Sapphire, you're really charming!

69
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:44,553
It's true!

70
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:48,026
You're so spunky, and you're just as tough as any boy!

71
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:50,446
Plus, you have such a kind heart!

72
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,360
So kind, so very kind!

73
00:04:54,575 --> 00:04:57,566
And the fact that you don't even realize it just makes you all the more charming!

74
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:00,166
I have a favor to ask of that kind Sapphire!

75
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:04,100
I want you to give that mysterious pen to the flaxen-haired girl!

76
00:05:04,870 --> 00:05:06,400
A flaxen-haired girl?

77
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:07,980
I want to know!

78
00:05:08,655 --> 00:05:10,240
How she really feels!

79
00:05:12,030 --> 00:05:13,100
I'll never forget!

80
00:05:13,970 --> 00:05:17,253
About the carnival where I danced with that flaxen-haired girl...

81
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:28,940
Young Franz... Is Sapphire that flaxen-haired girl?

82
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:32,920
Come on, please!

83
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
It's the favor of a lifetime!

84
00:05:34,285 --> 00:05:37,960
Find the flaxen-haired girl and tell her to write a letter with this pen!

85
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,680
Why don't you look for her and ask her yourself?

86
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:42,700
I can't!

87
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,326
My uncle's been breathing down my neck lately!

88
00:05:44,475 --> 00:05:46,640
I barely managed to sneak out of the castle today!

89
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:47,820
Prince Franz!

90
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,200
Prince Franz, you're making things very difficult for us!

91
00:05:55,565 --> 00:05:58,300
Sneaking off to play in the neighboring kingdom...

92
00:05:58,805 --> 00:06:00,920
His Majesty is looking for you!

93
00:06:01,295 --> 00:06:02,295
Please come back!

94
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:02,875
Oh no!

95
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,900
They found me already!

96
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,920
All right, Sapphire, I'm counting on you!

97
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,020
Don't forget!

98
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,070
Goodbye!

99
00:06:42,215 --> 00:06:44,120
Welcome back, Your Highness.

100
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:45,480
Oh dear, he's gone.

101
00:06:45,975 --> 00:06:48,360
Haha, hiding in the secret room again.

102
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:51,793
Dressing up like a girl right about now.

103
00:06:53,130 --> 00:06:57,200
Indeed, Master Sapphire is actually a girl, after all.

104
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,420
I wonder if Franz still hasn't figured it out.

105
00:07:08,270 --> 00:07:09,920
Maybe I'll write a letter to Franz.

106
00:07:10,245 --> 00:07:12,306
<i>From the girl with the flaxen hair</i>...

107
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,360
Hey, this is writing all by itself!

108
00:07:16,995 --> 00:07:20,780
The true identity of the girl with the flaxen hair is Sapphire.

109
00:07:21,305 --> 00:07:25,440
The girl with the flaxen hair is a little bit in love with Prince Franz.

110
00:07:25,730 --> 00:07:27,540
Oh dear, this is embarrassing!

111
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:29,100
I can't send a letter like this!

112
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:30,920
This really is a strange pen.

113
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:34,920
I know! It'd be fun to see what's on other people's minds.

114
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,680
Ah, it's Nanny!

115
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,800
Alright...

116
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:52,840
Up to mischief again?

117
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:54,540
What is this pen?

118
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:58,666
Just write whatever comes to mind.

119
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,960
Go on.

120
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,120
Is that so?

121
00:08:01,555 --> 00:08:05,840
<i>Master Sapphire goes too far with his mischief, so I can't stand him.</i>

122
00:08:06,473 --> 00:08:06,833
Here.

123
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:11,260
<i>May Master Sapphire grow up healthy and strong.</i>

124
00:08:13,565 --> 00:08:14,600
Thank you, Nanny.

125
00:08:22,110 --> 00:08:24,533
Just write down whatever is on your mind.

126
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:28,080
Well then: <i>Prince Sapphire is a splendid prince.</i>

127
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,720
<i>Long live Silverland!</i>

128
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,559
That is what was on my mind.

129
00:08:33,709 --> 00:08:36,679
<i>Gum, chocolate, juice, and ice cream</i>?

130
00:08:37,545 --> 00:08:39,860
You must be really hungry.

131
00:08:40,525 --> 00:08:42,733
Um, who's next?

132
00:08:42,859 --> 00:08:44,560
Oh, sorry!

133
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,300
Oh, Prince Sapphire.

134
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:49,026
That poor peacock.

135
00:08:49,051 --> 00:08:51,540
We must treat animals with kindness, you know.

136
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:53,920
Yes, yes.

137
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:57,146
So I won't forget, could you write that down here for me?

138
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,540
Yes, well then...

139
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:00,880
<i>Let us treat animals with kindness.</i>

140
00:09:01,734 --> 00:09:02,034
Here.

141
00:09:08,866 --> 00:09:11,940
<i>I'll secretly kill this peacock and use it as a hat decoration.</i>

142
00:09:12,053 --> 00:09:14,400
Oh my, did I write that?

143
00:09:17,656 --> 00:09:20,506
Knowing what people are really thinking is so much fun!

144
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:23,960
Though everyone thinks such awful things despite how they look.

145
00:09:25,911 --> 00:09:26,479
Alright,

146
00:09:26,503 --> 00:09:28,480
he's the one whose mind I want to read the most.

147
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:33,660
Ah, Prince Sapphire, what brings you here?

148
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,700
What are you thinking about right now?

149
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:36,641
Hmm, well,

150
00:09:36,665 --> 00:09:39,407
I was wishing for Prince Sapphire to grow up strong and for Silverland

151
00:09:39,431 --> 00:09:42,193
to prosper even more. Just something like that.

152
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:42,926
Wonderful!

153
00:09:43,195 --> 00:09:44,240
As expected of Lord Nylon!

154
00:09:44,609 --> 00:09:45,960
Write those words down right here!

155
00:09:46,145 --> 00:09:47,145
With pleasure.

156
00:09:47,589 --> 00:09:48,769
Yes, <i>scribble, scribble, scribble</i>...

157
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,526
Wait a minute...

158
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:59,320
Oh, my. Your Highness.

159
00:10:00,069 --> 00:10:01,360
Sorry, the rest is...

160
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,953
What on earth is going on?

161
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,140
<i>Sapphire must be a girl.</i>

162
00:10:08,444 --> 00:10:09,640
<i>Someday I'll rip off her mask...</i>

163
00:10:10,839 --> 00:10:11,860
I didn't write anything like that!

164
00:10:11,926 --> 00:10:12,738
I don't know, I really don't! 

165
00:10:12,762 --> 00:10:14,971
<i>Tonight at midnight.</i> That's as far as you wrote!

166
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:15,833
Nylon!

167
00:10:16,609 --> 00:10:18,293
Don't give me that I don't know!

168
00:10:18,349 --> 00:10:21,053
What on earth is happening at midnight tonight?!

169
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:21,486
I don't know.

170
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:22,560
I really have no...

171
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,586
Hey, wait!

172
00:10:25,298 --> 00:10:26,342
Wait Nylon!

173
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:27,426
I won't wait!

174
00:10:27,529 --> 00:10:28,380
I can't wait either!

175
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,400
I said wait!

176
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,099
Wait!

177
00:10:43,859 --> 00:10:44,900
We don't know where he's going.

178
00:10:44,983 --> 00:10:46,169
We'll cut him off!

179
00:10:57,315 --> 00:10:59,300
Well, welcome, Prince Sapphire.

180
00:10:59,895 --> 00:11:03,186
Grand Duke Duralumin, what are you planning to do at midnight tonight?

181
00:11:03,525 --> 00:11:05,333
Write your answer on paper with this pen!

182
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:08,240
No, I shall tell you out loud.

183
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:09,840
You can just make up lies out loud!

184
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,060
Write it with this pen!

185
00:11:11,205 --> 00:11:13,500
Unfortunately, I have an injury.

186
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,075
Then write with your left hand!

187
00:11:15,099 --> 00:11:19,319
My left hand is also, unfortunately... As I said, I'll answer out loud.

188
00:11:19,749 --> 00:11:21,120
You can say whatever you want out loud!

189
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,773
I don't want to hear your lies!

190
00:11:26,873 --> 00:11:30,382
Boy, what a pain to bring out a magic pen.

191
00:11:30,406 --> 00:11:32,300
No, wait, it's a wonderful pen.

192
00:11:32,465 --> 00:11:35,280
With that, even Sapphire won't be able to lie.

193
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:37,866
I'll make sure she writes "I am a woman".

194
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:38,500
Oh!

195
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:40,266
Brilliant as always, Grand Duke Duralumin!

196
00:11:40,514 --> 00:11:42,940
By the way, what about our plan for midnight?

197
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,540
Of course we're going through with it.

198
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,634
It'll be even more fun than the original plan.

199
00:12:06,879 --> 00:12:08,380
One hour left until midnight.

200
00:12:09,159 --> 00:12:11,020
What on earth are they up to?

201
00:12:16,839 --> 00:12:18,120
How many minutes are left?

202
00:12:26,289 --> 00:12:28,426
Ah, damn it! What happened?

203
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:52,960
Fire!

204
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:54,920
It won't open!

205
00:12:58,129 --> 00:12:59,600
I have to get out of here, quick!

206
00:13:02,999 --> 00:13:03,620
Fire!

207
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,960
Someone, help!

208
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:07,500
Guess we have no choice.

209
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,600
It's almost like they were waiting for this.

210
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:16,180
What are you doing?!

211
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,380
Quick, douse it with water!

212
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:21,141
Putting out the fire comes first... Leave it to me!

213
00:13:22,269 --> 00:13:23,269
They didn't even bring water?!

214
00:13:23,889 --> 00:13:27,180
I bet they're using the fire as cover to search my room.

215
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:29,780
Wait!

216
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,706
What kind of fire brigade doesn't bring water?!

217
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:32,940
What do you think you're doing?!

218
00:13:33,039 --> 00:13:34,880
Interfering with firefighting is a serious crime.

219
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:35,860
Shut up!

220
00:13:36,215 --> 00:13:38,140
You're fake firefighters!

221
00:13:38,459 --> 00:13:39,640
Do you want this place to burn?

222
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:42,240
Don't blame us if the castle turns to ash.

223
00:13:44,319 --> 00:13:45,420
It's spreading!

224
00:13:47,753 --> 00:13:48,546
Stop it!

225
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,886
Get out of here!

226
00:13:50,059 --> 00:13:53,734
How troublesome. Just leave it to us—or this axe might fly!

227
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,460
Why, you...

228
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:56,000
You're the ones who started the fire!

229
00:13:58,669 --> 00:13:59,669
You've shown your true colors!

230
00:14:11,086 --> 00:14:11,799
Hey!

231
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,346
Someone, help!

232
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:16,280
Hurry!

233
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:22,600
The fire brigade is here!

234
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:24,320
No water's coming out!

235
00:14:26,626 --> 00:14:27,626
One!

236
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:31,580
So cold!

237
00:14:38,975 --> 00:14:40,220
Thanks, Garigori!

238
00:14:40,245 --> 00:14:41,380
You guys...

239
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,040
Hey!

240
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,320
Wait!

241
00:14:47,245 --> 00:14:49,000
Give me a break!

242
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:49,455
Who is it?!

243
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,340
Your boss!

244
00:14:50,341 --> 00:14:54,420
It's someone I can't bring myself to say, lend me paper and a pen. I'll write their name down.

245
00:14:55,579 --> 00:14:58,020
<i>Let's make them write it with the magic pen.</i>

246
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:01,320
Come on!

247
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:02,360
Write it!

248
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,080
I got it!

249
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:07,170
I got it!

250
00:15:07,446 --> 00:15:08,646
Wait!

251
00:15:18,086 --> 00:15:18,900
Well done!

252
00:15:18,925 --> 00:15:19,653
Great job!

253
00:15:20,245 --> 00:15:23,560
Even you guys can be useful once in a while.

254
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:25,700
I guess so.

255
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,120
Now it's as good as ours.

256
00:15:28,655 --> 00:15:31,820
Tomorrow, I'll definitely tear off Sapphire's mask.

257
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:44,220
Does it still hurt?

258
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,420
Tink!

259
00:15:47,729 --> 00:15:48,800
Where on earth is this?

260
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,860
It's Mr. Garigori's room.

261
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:54,413
There was a fire in Sapphire's room yesterday, so I rushed right over.

262
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:56,820
And then Sapphire passed out.

263
00:15:57,399 --> 00:15:59,100
So, you took care of me the whole time?

264
00:15:59,335 --> 00:16:00,335
N-No...

265
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:03,646
Thank you.

266
00:16:04,709 --> 00:16:06,366
Is my secret room okay?

267
00:16:07,285 --> 00:16:09,840
It's fine. No one will ever find it.

268
00:16:10,435 --> 00:16:11,548
Ah, I'm so sleepy.

269
00:16:11,573 --> 00:16:12,900
Ah, Oh, no!

270
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:14,933
The pen!

271
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,480
Where did that thief go?!

272
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:18,766
Sapphire, what happened to the pen?

273
00:16:20,649 --> 00:16:22,520
It's something you were holding onto for Franz.

274
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:22,800
Yeah.

275
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:25,560
It was stolen during the fire last night.

276
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:27,000
That's a real problem.

277
00:16:30,875 --> 00:16:31,540
I wonder what it is?

278
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:33,760
Look at them moving all those desks and chairs.

279
00:16:43,621 --> 00:16:44,405
Your Highness!

280
00:16:44,430 --> 00:16:45,460
Sorry, sorry.

281
00:16:45,599 --> 00:16:46,800
What are they preparing for anyway?

282
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:47,433
Well...

283
00:16:47,485 --> 00:16:50,800
I don't know the details, but it's supposedly a ceremony for the Prince's Oath.

284
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,380
The Prince's Oath?

285
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:53,000
Yes!

286
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,460
The Prince's Oath?

287
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:54,880
A ceremony?

288
00:16:55,990 --> 00:16:56,990
The Prince's Oath, you say?

289
00:16:57,115 --> 00:16:58,360
Of course I know what that is.

290
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:04,260
It's a ceremony where the prince writes down and proclaims an oath to devote his life to the nation.

291
00:17:04,599 --> 00:17:07,219
Still, it hasn't been performed in nearly 200 years.

292
00:17:07,243 --> 00:17:10,119
This ceremony was abolished two centuries ago, so why bring it back so suddenly...?

293
00:17:10,619 --> 00:17:11,619
Prince Sapphire.

294
00:17:12,769 --> 00:17:16,280
Grand Duke Duralumin is waiting for you in the main hall.

295
00:17:16,645 --> 00:17:17,413
Duralumin?

296
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:18,420
What does he want?

297
00:17:18,679 --> 00:17:20,619
I was only told that he wishes to see you.

298
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:21,313
All right.

299
00:17:21,484 --> 00:17:22,484
I'll be right there.

300
00:17:30,504 --> 00:17:32,786
Congratulations, Your Highness.

301
00:17:32,999 --> 00:17:34,580
What's with all these over-the-top preparations?

302
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:38,513
Besides, why do I have to take the Prince's Oath anyway?

303
00:17:39,419 --> 00:17:42,440
Your Highness, this is an important ancient ritual.

304
00:17:43,079 --> 00:17:44,760
Indeed, indeed!

305
00:17:45,294 --> 00:17:46,599
What exactly am I supposed to do?

306
00:17:47,004 --> 00:17:47,860
It's quite simple.

307
00:17:47,974 --> 00:17:51,080
On this paper, you write: <i>I am without a doubt the prince of this realm</i>.

308
00:17:51,344 --> 00:17:54,100
From now on, I shall serve this kingdom as its prince.

309
00:17:54,499 --> 00:17:56,660
That is all you must write.

310
00:17:56,874 --> 00:17:58,140
Using that pen right there.

311
00:18:00,099 --> 00:18:01,498
<i>Oh, what a strange pen...</i>

312
00:18:01,522 --> 00:18:03,585
 Is something wrong, Prince Sapphire? 

313
00:18:03,609 --> 00:18:04,592
No!

314
00:18:04,616 --> 00:18:06,580
I just hate making such a big fuss over something so obvious.

315
00:18:07,999 --> 00:18:13,600
Your Highness, your father approved of this ritual himself and stamped it with his official seal.

316
00:18:13,874 --> 00:18:17,800
If you refuse, we'll make you do it by force.

317
00:18:25,919 --> 00:18:27,626
It starts right at noon.

318
00:18:27,669 --> 00:18:28,669
It's completely hopeless.

319
00:18:29,004 --> 00:18:32,520
If I use that pen, it'll definitely write "Sapphire is a woman"!

320
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:38,095
Oh, I know! Maybe Prince Franz can help us. 

321
00:18:38,119 --> 00:18:39,546
He won't be able to do a thing.

322
00:18:39,809 --> 00:18:40,920
Besides, there are only two hours left.

323
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:43,800
I can do it! I'll go to the neighboring kingdom.

324
00:18:44,549 --> 00:18:45,560
Ah, Tink!

325
00:18:46,869 --> 00:18:48,260
He'll never make it in time.

326
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,140
One hour left.

327
00:19:16,389 --> 00:19:17,480
We're here to escort you.

328
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:18,320
Escort?

329
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:19,420
Out of the way!

330
00:19:20,349 --> 00:19:22,300
It is time, Sapphire.

331
00:19:22,514 --> 00:19:23,560
To the Great Hall, please.

332
00:19:27,819 --> 00:19:28,819
Oh, what an oddball.

333
00:19:40,759 --> 00:19:43,520
Prince, please take that seat.

334
00:19:48,339 --> 00:19:49,360
Right over here.

335
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,680
Huge?

336
00:19:52,539 --> 00:19:53,720
Sapphire, what is the matter?

337
00:19:54,024 --> 00:19:57,180
Throwing a tantrum during such an important ceremony is unacceptable.

338
00:19:57,346 --> 00:19:57,820
Yes.

339
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:00,356
But... what happened?

340
00:20:00,464 --> 00:20:02,953
You're awfully reserved for a prince.

341
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,993
Sapphire, hurry and take your seat.

342
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:14,226
Now, please take the pen.

343
00:20:20,779 --> 00:20:21,779
Hurry up and write!

344
00:20:22,009 --> 00:20:24,680
Hesitating will only make them suspect you're a girl.

345
00:20:24,879 --> 00:20:28,500
Pull yourself together. Sapphire, take the pen.

346
00:20:29,329 --> 00:20:30,329
It's no use.

347
00:20:38,469 --> 00:20:41,060
Come on, fly faster, Oowashi-sans!

348
00:20:41,110 --> 00:20:42,469
Hurry, hurry!

349
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:43,080
Faster!

350
00:20:43,214 --> 00:20:44,280
There's no time left!

351
00:20:47,639 --> 00:20:49,100
Ah, I see it! The castle!

352
00:20:49,669 --> 00:20:52,200
Oowashi-sans, pull up to that window!

353
00:20:56,674 --> 00:20:57,860
Tink, let's go!

354
00:20:59,643 --> 00:21:02,506
I can't get down!

355
00:21:04,539 --> 00:21:06,310
What's wrong, Prince Sapphire?

356
00:21:06,334 --> 00:21:09,073
Is there some reason you can't take the oath?

357
00:21:09,224 --> 00:21:12,660
You're not a girl, so stop dragging your feet!

358
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:16,020
It's no use...

359
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:26,760
Oh no!

360
00:21:27,014 --> 00:21:28,400
Sapphire has the pen!

361
00:21:29,409 --> 00:21:30,233
Oh, what do we do?

362
00:21:30,260 --> 00:21:31,346
What are you talking about?

363
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:34,300
Times like this are when you should act like a man and knock 'em dead!

364
00:21:34,956 --> 00:21:36,659
I can't think of any good ideas.

365
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:37,593
Should I go make a scene?

366
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,710
Yeah, please!

367
00:21:41,274 --> 00:21:42,793
Hold it!

368
00:21:42,945 --> 00:21:43,705
Over there!

369
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:45,420
This way, this way!

370
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,580
Alright, cut it!

371
00:21:58,080 --> 00:21:59,080
Franz?

372
00:21:59,789 --> 00:22:02,440
I'm Blanco, and I travel the world picking fights!

373
00:22:02,999 --> 00:22:06,573
I heard Prince Sapphire is pretty strong in this kingdom, so I came to fight him.

374
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:08,680
Wh-What did you say?

375
00:22:08,764 --> 00:22:10,660
Seize this fool!

376
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:19,260
Come on, Sapphire!

377
00:22:19,709 --> 00:22:21,360
Sounds like fun. Let's do this!

378
00:22:22,439 --> 00:22:24,840
If anyone gets in the way of this fight, they'll regret it!

379
00:22:24,999 --> 00:22:27,433
Ugh, why did this guy have to butt in?

380
00:22:28,114 --> 00:22:29,140
Here I go!

381
00:22:33,309 --> 00:22:35,613
Thank you, Prince Franz.

382
00:22:47,753 --> 00:22:49,700
Hey, wait!

383
00:22:51,779 --> 00:22:53,260
Hey, wait! Stop!

384
00:22:56,069 --> 00:22:57,760
No way! Let me at 'em!

385
00:23:01,049 --> 00:23:02,880
Hold on! Had enough already?!

386
00:23:05,080 --> 00:23:06,080
Come here.

387
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,440
You're safe now.

388
00:23:22,504 --> 00:23:24,460
Now I can sleep soundly.

389
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:47,940
Franz, that strange pen of yours caused quite a lot of trouble.

390
00:23:48,549 --> 00:23:51,540
Sorry, sorry. I won't rely on something like this again.

391
00:23:52,504 --> 00:23:56,986
Hey Franz, people say one thing and mean another, don't they?

392
00:23:58,079 --> 00:24:00,740
Yeah. I wonder if that flaxen-haired girl lies, too.

393
00:24:02,699 --> 00:24:05,760
No, I'm sure she's the one who tells the truth.

394
00:24:06,164 --> 00:24:07,360
I'm sure you'll meet her soon.

395
00:24:08,020 --> 00:24:09,153
Wait, really?

396
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:10,340
You reached her, right?

397
00:24:13,509 --> 00:24:14,679
He still hasn't noticed.

398
00:24:19,284 --> 00:24:21,284

